    "//geometry.donkey": "DonkeyModel.createBodyLayer chain is AbstractEquineModel.createBodyMesh(NONE) .apply(DONKEY_TRANSFORMER) .apply(MeshTransformer.scaling(0.87)). Bytecode tooling captures the base mesh + final scaling but misses the DONKEY_TRANSFORMER.modifyMesh step which addOrReplaceChild replaces the base horse ears with taller donkey ears (cube -1,-7,0 size 2,7,1 uv 0,12) at PartPose.offsetAndRotation(1.25,-10,4, pi/12, 0, \u00b1pi/12), and also adds left_chest / right_chest body children (the latter are hidden by the harness DonkeyModelMixin at zero state so neither pipeline renders them). Ear PartPose is baked here: cube origin gets the ear offset baked in (-1+1.25, -7-10, 0+4) = (0.25, -17, 4) for left; cube.pivot + cube.rotation = (15X, 0, \u00b115Z) so the kit applies the ear's own rotation around the ear anchor before the bone chain's 30X head_parts rotation. cube.pivot is in BONE-LOCAL coords = DONKEY_SCALE * ear_offset = (\u00b11.0875, -8.7, 3.48). The kit's vanilla-shape T(p)*R bone chain + T(+cp)*R*T(-cp) cube-pivot composition produces bit-identical output to the previous absolute-frame chain.",
